<meta type=article>
  <title | Hash-sigil heading dispatch fixture>
  <author | Test Author>
</meta>

<# Plain hash-sigil section #>

This top-level section is authored with the `<#>` sigil form rather than the
named `<section>` form. It should produce an eHTML `<section>` element with a
proper `<section-title>`, not an unknown-element span.

<# #sec:intro | Hash-sigil section with id #>

The id attribute on the sigil-form section must thread through to the section
node so that `<ref @sec:intro>` can resolve to it.

<## Sub-section with *emphasis* in the title ##>

The double-hash sigil produces a `<sub-section>`. The emphasis in the title
text must be recursively parsed — proving `isOpaqueContent: false` for hash
sigils.

<### Sub-sub-section with `inline code` ###>

The triple-hash sigil produces a `<sub-sub-section>`. The inline code in the
title text must also be recursively parsed.
